An absolute `--target` ending in the machine's declared `artifact:` implies the workdir the artifact
hangs off, so hooks run there even though the command was invoked elsewhere. The target is written
`~/…`, which `--target` expands against the sandbox's `home` root.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-hooks
title: Hooks
summary: Hook-bearing fixture for playbook-transition.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  only: []

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: noted
            when: the environment is recorded
            hooks: ["script env-note"]
      noted: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/only/prompt.md --
---
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/_scripts/env-note --
#!/bin/sh
{
  echo "artifact=$BOOPING_ARTIFACT"
  echo "workdir=$BOOPING_WORKDIR"
  echo "cwd=$(pwd)"
} > "$BOOPING_WORKDIR/env.txt"
-- fixtures/home/run/index.md --
---
status: intaking
---
-- cmd --
chmod +x ../home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/_scripts/env-note
booping playbook-transition fx-hooks noted --target ~/run/index.md
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
intaking → noted
frontmatter: status=noted
script env-note: ok
-- stderr --
-- expected/home/run/env.txt --
artifact={HOME}/run/index.md
workdir={HOME}/run
cwd={HOME}/run
